#
# Sval is a v1 platform on Windows as well as macOS. Without this file, a
# Windows clone with the default core.autocrlf=true converts these to CRLF,
# and `git apply` of an LF patch against an LF upstream checkout then rejects.
*.patch text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
series text eol=lf

# Every pull request that adds a patch appends one line to the series, and
# two appends at one place are a conflict to plain three-way merge. `union`
# keeps both lines. Forgejo checks pull requests with `git merge-tree` in a
# bare repository, which reads this file only with `attr.tree = HEAD` in its
# git config; the server sets that. Two patches whose order matters still
# fail in `apply-patches.sh`, not silently.
patches/series merge=union
